    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Fee in question: {{ $json.output.fee_issue.fee_name }}\nConfusion seen in user reviews: {{ $json.output.fee_issue.confusion_summary }}\n\nWrite a customer-support explanation of this fee.\n\nRules:\n- MAXIMUM 6 bullet points.\n- Neutral, facts-only tone. No marketing language and no promises.\n- Cover what the fee is, when it applies, how it is calculated, and where the rate for a specific scheme is stated (in the scheme's official documents).\n- Describe only how exit load works in general, based on the sources below.\n- Do NOT say anything about what any app shows or where an app lists information.\n- Do NOT mention Key Information Memorandum (KIM). Refer only to the Scheme Information Document.\n- Mention SEBI only to say it sets a maximum limit on exit load. Do not state the limit.\n- For SIPs, say only that each instalment is treated as a separate purchase with its own holding period.\n- Do NOT use bold, asterisks or any markdown symbols anywhere.\n- Do NOT put URLs inside the bullets. Put them only in the \"Sources:\" list.\n- If a fact is not supported by these sources, do not state it.\n\nOutput format:\n- (up to 6 bullets, each starting with \"- \")\n\nSources:\n1. https://mf.nipponindiaim.com/investoreducation/financial-term-of-the-week-exit-load\n2. https://www.sebi.gov.in/sebi_data/meetingfiles/sep-2025/1758696854726_1.pdf\n\nThe final line of your answer must be exactly: Last checked: {{ $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd') }}",
        "batching": {}
      },
